---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Generate QR codes locally in your browser" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f8fafc" />
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' blob: data:; connect-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'" />
    <title>QR Code Generator</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="h-16 bg-brand px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="mx-auto flex h-full max-w-5xl items-center justify-center">
        <img class="h-10 w-auto object-contain" src="images/one-logotype-white.png" alt="ONE" />
      </div>
    </header>
    <main class="bg-page px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 sm:py-12">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <header>
          <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text sm:text-3xl">Create a safe QR code</h1>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted">Standard QR code follows ISO/IEC 18004:2024</p>
        </header>
        <nav class="mt-8 flex border-b border-border" aria-label="QR generator sections">
          <button id="tab-generator" class="border-b-2 border-brand px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-brand" aria-current="page" type="button">Generator</button>
          <button id="tab-usage" class="px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-text-muted" type="button">Usage</button>
        </nav>

        <section id="usage-panel" class="hidden mt-8 space-y-12" data-testid="usage-guide">
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-overall-heading">
            <h2 id="usage-overall-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Overall</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">This guideline defines the technical implementation requirements for the QR codes this tool generates for ONE digital products and customer communications. Every QR code is built entirely in your browser: the payload is never sent to a server.</p>
            <ol class="mt-5 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-base leading-6 text-text-muted sm:grid-cols-4">
              <li><strong class="text-text">1. Choose the context. </strong>Select Digital for screen-to-phone journeys or Print for physical materials.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-text">2. Choose the profile. </strong>Match the variant to the placement and expected scanning distance.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-text">3. Review the result. </strong>Check the selected version, contrast, quiet zone, and logo status in the preview.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-text">4. Export and test. </strong>Use SVG when you need scalable artwork; use PNG when you need a ready-made raster file.</li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-principal-heading">
            <h2 id="usage-principal-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Principal</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
              <div><div class="flex h-20 items-center"><img class="h-20 w-20 object-contain" src="images/qr-sample.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" /></div><h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-text">Brand consistency</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">QR codes present a consistent appearance across ONE products: ONE magenta <code>#BD0F72</code> by default or black, rounded modules with standard square finders, an opaque white background, and the bundled ONE lettermark when the selected version supports it.</p></div>
              <div><div class="flex h-20 items-center"><img class="h-20 w-20 object-contain" src="images/scan-icon.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" /></div><h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-text">Technical precision</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Successful scanning depends on adequate contrast and clear space. Every export enforces a 4.5:1 minimum foreground/background contrast ratio and a 4-module quiet zone automatically; there is no way to configure an unsafe combination in this tool.</p></div>
              <div><div class="flex h-20 items-center"><img class="h-20 w-20 object-contain" src="images/accessibility-icon.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" /></div><h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-text">Accessibility</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Everyone should be able to reach the same destination regardless of whether they can scan the code. Always pair a placed QR code with a visible link, button, or instructions as a fallback.</p></div>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-when-heading">
            <h2 id="usage-when-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">When to use</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Use a QR code when it provides a clear, meaningful bridge between where someone is now and a digital destination. The right output variant depends on whether the code is shown on a screen or printed.</p>
            <div class="mt-6 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">1. Digital</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Use a QR code in a digital interface when the destination is meant to be opened on a different device.</p><ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc text-base leading-7 text-text-muted"><li>Continue an activity on a mobile device</li><li>Open a mobile-specific experience</li><li>Transfer a URL, session, or information from desktop to mobile</li><li>Pair or connect a device</li></ul></div>
              <div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">2. Print</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Use a QR code in physical materials when it provides a convenient bridge from the physical experience to a digital destination.</p><ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc text-base leading-7 text-text-muted"><li>Posters and signage</li><li>Printed documents: brochures, flyers, business cards, packaging</li><li>Exhibition and event materials, product or service information</li><li>Shipment or logistics documents</li></ul></div>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-10 text-base font-semibold text-text">3. Quick decision rule</h3>
            <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full min-w-[38rem] border-collapse text-base"><thead><tr class="border-b border-border bg-surface text-left text-sm font-semibold text-text-muted"><th class="px-3 py-3 pr-4">Context</th><th class="px-3 py-3 pr-4">Use the QR code?</th><th class="px-3 py-3">Interaction</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-border"><tr><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4 text-text">Desktop -&gt; Mobile</td><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4"><span class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-800">YES</span></td><td class="px-3 py-3 text-text-muted">QR code</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4 text-text">Mobile -&gt; Desktop</td><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4"><span class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-red-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-red-800">NO</span></td><td class="px-3 py-3 text-text-muted">Link or button</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4 text-text">Printed material -&gt; Digital page</td><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4"><span class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-800">YES</span></td><td class="px-3 py-3 text-text-muted">QR code</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4 text-text">Desktop -&gt; App download</td><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4"><span class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-800">YES</span></td><td class="px-3 py-3 text-text-muted">QR code and visible link</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4 text-text">Mobile -&gt; App download</td><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4"><span class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-red-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-red-800">NO</span></td><td class="px-3 py-3 text-text-muted">App Store or Google Play button</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4 text-text">Digital UI -&gt; Digital page</td><td class="px-3 py-3 pr-4"><span class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-red-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-red-800">NO</span></td><td class="px-3 py-3 text-text-muted">Link or button</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
          </section>
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-anatomy-heading"><h2 id="usage-anatomy-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Anatomy</h2><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Every generated symbol is a regular square array of modules made of function patterns - quiet zone, finder patterns, separators, timing patterns, and format/version information - surrounding an encoding region of data and error-correction codewords. Function modules are never repurposed to carry data or logo pixels.</p><div class="mt-6 flex justify-center"><img class="w-full max-w-3xl rounded-lg border border-border object-contain" src="images/qr-anatomy-diagram.png" alt="Diagram of a QR code labeling its quiet zone, finder pattern, separator, version info, and data/error-correction codewords" /></div></section>
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-rules-heading"><h2 id="usage-rules-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Standard generation rule</h2><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">The renderer keeps the QR structure safe and deterministic. You can choose the context, output profile, foreground preset, and whether the bundled logo is enabled; the rules below describe what the generated artifact does with those choices.</p><h3 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold text-text">1. Generation specifications</h3><div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full min-w-[42rem] border-collapse text-base"><thead><tr class="border-b border-border bg-surface text-left text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-text-muted"><th class="px-3 py-2 pr-4">Property</th><th class="px-3 py-2">Standard</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-border"><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">QR standard</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">ISO/IEC 18004:2024</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Export format</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">SVG or PNG</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Error correction</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">M by default; H automatically when the ONE logo is enabled</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Quiet zone</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">4 modules on every side</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">ONE logo</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">Bundled ONE lettermark, available from Version 6 through Version 11; automatically omitted at Version 12 and above so the payload is never lost</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Colors</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">ONE magenta <code>#BD0F72</code> (default) or black <code>#000000</code>, always on an opaque white background</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Generator</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-text-muted">This QR Generation Tool - runs entirely in your browser, no upload</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2"><div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">Encoding and payload</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">The exact input is preserved in the browser. Empty input is rejected; UTF-8 is used for non-ASCII text with ECI assignment 26, and the encoded byte count is used for Byte mode. Numeric, alphanumeric, and byte segments are selected deterministically when that saves space. A payload must fit the maximum version supported by the selected profile; otherwise the tool reports a capacity error.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">Branding and fallback</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">The bundled ONE lettermark is enabled by default. Logo mode uses ECC H and starts at Version 6; it is placed only when the knockout avoids every function module. Unsafe or out-of-range branding falls back to the same exact-payload symbol without a logo. Turning the logo off uses ECC M and ordinary version fitting.</p></div></div></section>
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-sizes-heading"><h2 id="usage-sizes-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Size and version recommendations</h2><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">Pick the output variant that matches where the code is used. Each profile fixes its canvas size and approved QR version range, so a larger payload may need a profile with a wider range. The preview reports the selected version and whether the payload fits.</p><h3 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold text-text">2. Size and version recommendations</h3><div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full min-w-[54rem] border-collapse text-base"><thead><tr class="border-b border-border bg-surface text-left text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-text-muted"><th class="px-3 py-2 pr-4">Type</th><th class="px-3 py-2 pr-4">Usage</th><th class="px-3 py-2 pr-4">Recommended size</th><th class="px-3 py-2">QR version range</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-border"><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Digital</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Small - web footer, secondary CTA</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">100 x 100 px</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V5 - V6</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Digital</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Standard - general web content</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">120 x 120 px</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V5 - V8</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Digital</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Primary CTA - download app, continue on mobile</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">160 x 160 px</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V5 - V12</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Digital</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Hero / Campaign - landing page, campaign</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">200 x 200 px</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V8 - V12</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Print</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Business card</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">25 mm</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V5 - V12, test in actual print</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Print</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Flyer / Brochure</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">30 mm</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V5 - V12, test in actual print</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Print</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">Poster / Package</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">40 mm</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">V5 - V12, test in actual print, consider material surface</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="mt-2 text-xs text-text-muted">Print sizes are 150 dpi artifact conversions, not a physical-size guarantee. Always test the exported file on the final material, device, and viewing distance before shipping it.</p><div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2"><div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">PNG: 3x export resolution</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">The PNG canvas is exactly three times the matching SVG/base canvas: for example, a 120 x 120 px Standard SVG exports as a 360 x 360 px PNG. This is a higher-resolution raster export, not a guarantee that the visible QR symbol itself is exactly three times larger for every QR version.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">SVG: scale for the final placement</h3><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">SVG is vector-based and can be scaled proportionally without losing edge quality. Keep the complete SVG, including its four-module quiet zone, and choose a physical or on-screen size that matches the scanning distance. Never crop, stretch non-uniformly, or rasterize it below a suitable resolution.</p></div></div></section>
          <section aria-labelledby="usage-signage-heading"><h2 id="usage-signage-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Large signage: use viewing distance, not pixels</h2><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-text-muted">This tool does not encode a physical size - it exports SVG or PNG pixels. For large-format displays or signage, choose a physical print size using the scanner's expected distance rather than picking pixels alone, then export SVG and scale it to that size.</p><table class="mt-5 w-full max-w-md border-collapse text-base"><thead><tr class="border-b border-border text-left text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-text-muted"><th class="py-2 pr-4">Viewing distance</th><th class="py-2">Approx. QR size</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-border"><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">0.5 m</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">50 mm</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">1 m</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">100 mm</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">2 m</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">200 mm</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">3 m</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">300 mm</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">5 m</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">500 mm</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-text-muted">10 m</td><td class="py-2 text-text-muted">1000 mm</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
        </section>

        <div id="generator-panel" class="mt-6 grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,3fr)_minmax(20rem,2fr)]">
          <section aria-labelledby="settings-heading">
            <h2 id="settings-heading" class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Settings</h2>
            <label for="base-url" class="mt-4 block text-sm font-semibold text-text">Base URL <span class="text-brand">*</span></label>
            <input id="base-url" type="url" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-page px-3 py-2 text-sm text-text outline-none focus:border-focus focus:ring-2 focus:ring-focus/20" placeholder="E.g. https://example.com/promo" autocomplete="url" aria-describedby="base-url-counts url-validation" />
            <p id="base-url-counts" class="mt-1 text-xs text-text-muted">0 characters | 0 UTF-8 bytes</p>
            <p id="url-validation" class="mt-2 min-h-5 text-sm font-semibold text-red-700" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <section class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-surface p-4" aria-labelledby="utm-heading">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4"><h3 id="utm-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-text">UTM Configuration</h3><label class="relative inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center"><input id="utm-enabled" class="peer sr-only" type="checkbox" checked aria-label="Enable UTM configuration" /><span class="pointer-events-none h-5 w-9 rounded-full bg-text-muted transition peer-checked:bg-brand after:absolute after:left-0.5 after:top-0.5 after:h-4 after:w-4 after:rounded-full after:bg-page after:transition peer-checked:after:translate-x-4"></span><span class="sr-only">Enable UTM configuration</span></label></div>
              <div id="utm-fields" class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2"><label class="block text-xs font-semibold text-text">utm_source<input id="utm-source" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-page px-3 py-2 text-sm outline-none focus:border-focus focus:ring-2 focus:ring-focus/20" aria-label="utm_source" placeholder="Where the scan comes from" /></label><label class="block text-xs font-semibold text-text">utm_medium<input id="utm-medium" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-page px-3 py-2 text-sm outline-none focus:border-focus focus:ring-2 focus:ring-focus/20" aria-label="utm_medium" placeholder="The channel" /></label><label class="block text-xs font-semibold text-text sm:col-span-2">utm_campaign<input id="utm-campaign" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-page px-3 py-2 text-sm outline-none focus:border-focus focus:ring-2 focus:ring-focus/20" aria-label="utm_campaign" placeholder="Campaign name" /></label></div>
              <div id="custom-params" class="mt-4 grid gap-3"></div><button id="add-param" class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-brand hover:text-brand-dark" type="button">+ Add Parameter</button>
            </section>
            <label for="encoded-url" class="mt-4 block text-sm font-semibold text-text">Encoded URL <span class="font-normal italic text-text-muted">- Automatic generation</span></label><textarea id="encoded-url" class="mt-1 min-h-20 w-full resize-none rounded-md border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-2 text-sm text-text" rows="3" readonly></textarea><p id="encoded-url-guidance" class="mt-1 text-xs text-text-muted">The encoded URL will appear after the base URL is valid.</p>
          </section>
          <section class="rounded-lg bg-surface p-4" aria-labelledby="preview-heading">
            <h2 id="preview-heading" class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Preview</h2>
            <fieldset class="mt-4"><legend class="text-xs font-semibold text-text">QR Type <span class="text-brand">*</span></legend><div class="mt-1 flex gap-4 text-sm"><label class="flex items-center gap-2"><input type="radio" name="qr-type" value="digital" checked />Digital</label><label class="flex items-center gap-2"><input type="radio" name="qr-type" value="print" />Print</label></div></fieldset>
            <label for="profile-select" class="mt-3 block text-xs font-semibold text-text">Output variant</label><select id="profile-select" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-page px-3 py-2 text-sm outline-none focus:border-focus focus:ring-2 focus:ring-focus/20" aria-label="Output variant"><option value="small">Small</option><option value="standard" selected>Standard</option><option value="primary-cta">Primary CTA</option><option value="hero-campaign">Hero / Campaign</option><option value="business-card">Business card</option><option value="flyer-brochure">Flyer / Brochure</option><option value="poster-package">Poster / Package</option></select>
            <fieldset class="mt-4"><legend class="text-xs font-semibold text-text">Color type <span class="text-brand">*</span></legend><div class="mt-1 flex gap-4 text-sm"><label class="flex items-center gap-2"><input type="radio" name="foreground-theme" value="magenta" checked />Magenta</label><label class="flex items-center gap-2"><input type="radio" name="foreground-theme" value="black" />Black</label></div></fieldset>
            <label class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold text-text"><span>ONE logo in QR</span><input id="bundled-logo" type="checkbox" aria-label="ONE logo in QR" checked /></label>
            <div id="qr-preview" class="mt-4 grid min-h-72 place-items-center rounded-lg border border-border bg-page p-4" data-testid="qr-preview" role="img" aria-label="QR code preview unavailable"><p id="preview-placeholder" class="max-w-56 text-center text-sm text-text-muted">Enter a valid URL to see the QR preview.</p></div>
            <p id="caution" class="mt-3 min-h-5 text-xs font-semibold text-amber-800" role="status"></p><div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><button id="download-png" class="rounded-md border border-brand bg-page px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-brand disabled:border-border disabled:text-text-muted" data-testid="download-png" type="button" disabled>Download PNG</button><button id="download-svg" class="rounded-md bg-brand px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white disabled:bg-border disabled:text-text-muted" data-testid="download-svg" type="button" disabled>Download SVG</button></div><p id="export-status" class="mt-2 text-xs text-text-muted" role="status">Enter a URL to generate a QR code.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
